Data Backup Strategies

Data backup is critical during cloud migration to ensure data integrity, prevent loss, and enable seamless recovery. Below are the backup strategies for key components during the migration from Azure to Alibaba Cloud:

Databases (e.g., SQL Database)





Tool: Use Database Backup Service (DBS) for real-time incremental backups of databases like MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server.



Strategy:





Perform full backups at the start of the migration and daily incremental backups to ensure data integrity.



Enable Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR) for continuous backups, allowing restoration to any specific time within the retention period.



Retain backups for at least 30 days or as per compliance requirements.



Details: DBS supports both homogeneous (e.g., MySQL to MySQL) and heterogeneous (e.g., Oracle to PolarDB) migrations, reducing downtime and ensuring data consistency.

Object Storage (e.g., Blob Storage)





Tool: Use Object Storage Service (OSS) for storing and managing unstructured data.



Strategy:





Enable continuous replication from Azure Blob Storage to Alibaba Cloud OSS using tools like Data Transmission Service (DTS) or third-party solutions.



Schedule weekly backups for less frequently accessed data.



Enable versioning in OSS to maintain historical versions of objects.



Details: OSS supports lifecycle management, allowing data to transition to lower-cost storage classes (e.g., Archive) based on access frequency, optimizing costs during migration.

Virtual Machines (e.g., Virtual Machines)





Tool: Use Cloud Backup for backing up Elastic Compute Service (ECS) instances.



Strategy:





Schedule daily snapshots of ECS instances and attached volumes to capture the VM state.



Retain snapshots for at least 7-14 days, depending on recovery objectives.



Details: Cloud Backup supports deduplication and AES-256 encryption, ensuring secure and cost-effective storage during migration.

Additional Tools





Hybrid Backup Recovery (HBR): Useful for backing up on-premises or third-party cloud data to Alibaba Cloud, though less relevant for Azure-to-Alibaba Cloud migration since both are cloud environments.



Third-Party Tools: Consider tools like Rubrik for multi-cloud support, zero-trust architecture, and advanced encryption to enhance backup security.

